String models can be tested against the process \(e^{+}e^{-}\to q\overline{q}\) at high energies. This allows to study string fragmentation without the uncertainties introduced from a hadronic initial state. Nucleon-nucleon collisions are then described by fragmentation of strings, i.e. nucleons excited in the inelastic collisions. The mechanisms for

