Figure (4.1) shows the layout of RHIC complex. The path of the Au atoms begins in the Pulsed Sputter Ion Source in the Tandem Van de Graaff facility with a charge of -1. These atoms are accelerated and passed through two thin Au foils that strip the Au atoms of some electrons, leaving them with a net charge of +32. The Booster Synchrotron takes the 1 MeV/u Au beam and accelerates it to 95 MeV/u and further strips the ions to a net charge of +77. The beam is then fed into the AGS where it is bunched and accelerated to 10.8 GeV/u.

